\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{clifford}

\taxon{Theorem}
\title{The exterior Clifford action \citet{Section 3.2.2, Proposition 3.5, p. 57}{meinrenken2013clifford}}
\lean/tauceti{TauCeti.spinAction}

\p{The square relation of \ref{fcap-001J} extends uniquely to an algebra
homomorphism

##{\rho:\Cl(Q)\longrightarrow\operatorname{End}_K(S).}

On the three summands it is determined by

##{\rho(\iota(x))s=x\wedge s,\qquad
\rho(\iota(y))s=\iota_y(s),\qquad
\rho(\iota(z))s=\ell(z)\alpha(s).}

The corresponding formalized equations are
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.spinAction_ι_wedge},
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.spinAction_ι_contract}, and
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.spinAction_ι_lineOperator}.
Chevalley's split even-dimensional model has no remainder term; the third
formula is TauCeti's odd-line extension of that construction.}
